      "name": "test_bed",
      "comment": "A single-wheel test bed: the small plain rigid wheel of P.G. Kumar and S. Jayalekshmi (J. Theoretical and Applied Mechanics 57(3), 2019), 160 mm by 32 mm under 52.2 N, on their TRI-1 lunar soil simulant. They measured 2.66 mm of sinkage, but Bekker's law with the moduli they give for the soil carries only a third of the weight at that sinkage, and the wheel sinks about 11 mm here. The carriage is held at 0.05 m/s and the wheel at -0.78125 rad/s, 20% slip, by PI controllers; the hanger, with the wheel, is free to sink. Ground at z = 0, z down.",
